13596	{"artifactId":"LLD-a8c4399a90185f7f-s1","entry":{"id":"review-8a3971593f7b8ebd8ecb0f5c73747a89","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:20:57.002Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed scope covers the approved issue's budget, filtering, observability and rollout intent.","evidence":"The approved ISSUE specifies inclusive accounting across retry/gather/relation/comparison paths, flat JSONL exclusion, content-free call outcomes and daemon update before TU1 retry. Sections 2–7 address these and preserve the configuration, timeout and TU1 non-goals. The native hard-ceiling interpretation is explicitly left for approval. [files: docs/standalone/enforce-all-inclusive-review-budgets-exclude-E20261027ecf8440c/ISSUE.md, .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-ecf8440c29a6aa99.json]","action":"Resolve Q-native-ceiling before implementation as the design requires.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Current review admission measures enveloped prompt text rather than an inclusive request budget.","evidence":"reviewLimitChars returns readReviewChunkTokens(configPath) * 3 with a default of 128000. job.ts measures promptChars(envelopeMessages(...)); the driver supplies call.schema separately. Ollama's review session accumulates tool history and then appends a schema-bearing final instruction without a context-budget guard. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/limit.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/envelope.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts, src/agent/providers/ollama.ts, src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts]","action":"Replace admission comparisons while retaining promptChars as a diagnostic.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The existing splitter can be reused unchanged while preserving all required evidence.","evidence":"prepare.ts identifies calls/references as required neighbours, but its overflow fallback says 'the summaries that do not fit are left out' and repeatedly executes neighbours = neighbours.slice(0, -1). pipeline-job.test.ts explicitly asserts 'only the summaries that fit'. This contradicts the design's no-required-evidence-omission guarantee under the smaller inclusive allowance. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/prepare.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/__tests__/pipeline-job.test.ts]","action":"Specify a change to this fallback: refuse or preserve the required relationship evidence through a supported alternative. Update the existing omission-expecting regression.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The serial driver and managed inspection/final-answer helpers exist with compatible extension seams.","evidence":"runReviewJob selects calls[0] and awaits it before advancing. runReadOnlyToolLoop accepts ReadOnlyToolLoopArgs and retains accumulated messages; emitStructuredAnswer accepts StructuredAnswerArgs and appends the closing instruction. Neither argument interface currently includes reviewBudget. Gather and duplicate adapters have separate message-only sentChars helpers, as described. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts, src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/adapters/code-review-gather.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/adapters/code-review-duplicates.ts]","action":"Reuse these seams with optional review-only options and one shared estimator.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The contract specifies how provider-specific wire accounting becomes available during initial planning.","evidence":"createReviewJob receives adapter, path, snapshot, limitChars and options, but no provider. Actual callers construct the job before passing the provider to runReviewJob. CliProvider separately transforms Codex schemas through codexSchemaJson(schema), while Claude sends JSON.stringify(schema). The design requires provider-qualified planning but does not define the preparation/profile interface or how callers supply it; deriving the default solely from review configuration cannot identify the selected provider's wire transformation. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/code-review.ts, src/workflow/review/review.ts, src/workflow/review/template-review.ts, src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts]","action":"Define a provider preparation or conservative-profile contract and its ownership. Include propagation through code-review, grounded review and template-review entry points, with matching planning/dispatch tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The shared generated-file filter is a valid seam for subject and material exclusion.","evidence":"resolveCodeReviewSubject passes LEDGER_EXCLUDE_GLOBS into changedFiles before constructing subject.changedFiles. changedFiles forwards its exclusion globs to staged, unstaged and committed-unit/range diffs. Existing real-git attribution tests also exercise diff grounding with that same constant. The current constant includes '.insrc/artifacts/*.json' and lacks JSONL. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/changed-files.ts, src/workflow/code-review/subject.ts, src/workflow/code-review/runner.ts, src/workflow/code-review/__tests__/diff-attribution.test.ts]","action":"Add the flat JSONL glob at this seam and retain the proposed nested-file and freshness regressions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The stale-state migration identifies the actual persisted admission state and its rejection boundary.","evidence":"The inspected entry points create local ReviewPipelineJob values. The code-review step's stored payload contains subject and grounding, rather than a ReviewPipelineJob or saved admission policy. The design describes an 'in-flight serialized review job' but names no serializer, loader or resume entry point for it. Analyzer output did not establish persistence or recovery behavior either. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/types.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/code-review.ts, src/workflow/review/review.ts, src/workflow/review/template-review.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/types.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/state-store.ts]","action":"Identify the concrete persisted/resumed state and validation boundary, or document that pipeline jobs are not persisted and scope stale-state handling to the actual controller state.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed relationship documentation adequately describes internal ownership without requiring an ERD or UX mock.","evidence":"Section 3.3 identifies job-to-policy ownership, job-to-call cardinality, one admission breakdown per call, managed-turn rechecks and provider copy semantics. These correspond to the existing adapter/job/driver/provider boundaries. The generated sequence companion contains the planner, policy, serial driver, provider and logging interactions. No user-facing layout or persistent entity relationship is introduced. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/types.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts, docs/standalone/enforce-all-inclusive-review-budgets-exclude-E20261027a8c4399a/S001/sequence-diagram.html]","action":"Keep the ownership prose and companion synchronized with the provider preparation contract once specified.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.2","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The generated sequence companion renders consistently with its source.","evidence":"The linked HTML exists and contains inline Mermaid source, participant descriptions, bundled rendering code and a render-error fallback. Its source describes the proposed accounting flow. No local Playwright or Puppeteer package resolved during renderer discovery; no rendered browser output was obtained, so layout, legibility and successful Mermaid execution remain unverified. [files: docs/standalone/enforce-all-inclusive-review-budgets-exclude-E20261027a8c4399a/S001/sequence-diagram.html]","action":"Render the existing companion and inspect its SVG, labels and fit-to-view behavior before claiming visual verification.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"New budget failures have an explicit fail-closed integration with existing retry and partial-result policies.","evidence":"driver.ts classifies every unrecognized error as 'transient'. applyFailure retries transient errors and can subsequently record-not-judged or record-observation instead of throwing; the grounded design-review verify stage uses record-not-judged. The design introduces ReviewBudgetError and promises 'fail once' and no successful refused execution, but does not specify bypassing this classifier and stage policy. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/design-review.ts]","action":"Define a typed budget-error branch before generic classification that preserves the cause and terminates without retry or partial-success conversion, except for explicitly supported evidence-preserving replanning.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The existing correction fallback is compatible with the proposed refusal-on-overflow behavior.","evidence":"applyFailure explicitly says 'A correction that would not fit the limit is left out' and reissues call.prompt when sentChars(corrected) exceeds the limit. A final dispatch check would therefore see the smaller uncorrected request rather than detect the rejected correction's overflow. The design does not explicitly replace this branch despite requiring a correction overflow to replan or fail. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts]","action":"Specify replacement of the correction-dropping branch with inclusive correction admission and explicit refusal/replanning. Add a regression proving the original prompt is not reissued without required correction.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.3","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Content-free lifecycle events alone establish the promised absence of source-bearing error telemetry.","evidence":"The driver's existing failure log includes detail from err.message. CliProvider.runReviewSession logs 'err: msg' for stalls even when internalRetry is false, before rethrowing. Thus sanitized new lifecycle events would coexist with raw error logging unless these paths are explicitly changed; the design's logging plan does not identify that review-scoped suppression/redaction work. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts, src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts]","action":"Specify review-scoped allowlisted error logging across driver and provider failure paths, and capture all relevant logger output in the sentinel-leak test.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed test strategy maps the issue's substantive acceptance behaviors to appropriate deterministic seams.","evidence":"The strategy covers inclusive boundaries, schema normalization, managed history growth, serial retries, JSONL filtering, lifecycle outcomes and compatibility. Existing pipeline-job tests provide scripted adapters/providers; source-inspection tests assert session routing, deadlines and no structured fallback; CLI session tests use fake subprocesses; diff-attribution tests use real temporary Git repositories. These support the proposed test approach, though the proposed new tests have not been implemented or run in this review. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/__tests__/pipeline-job.test.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/__tests__/code-review-source-inspection.test.ts, src/agent/providers/__tests__/cli-review-session.test.ts, src/workflow/code-review/__tests__/diff-attribution.test.ts]","action":"Extend these suites with the identified neighbour-omission, correction-overflow, fail-closed budget-error and provider-log sentinel regressions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":3,"med":2,"low":8,"unverified":2},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T05:20:57.002Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
