612	{"artifactId":"LLD-a8c4399a90185f7f-s1","entry":{"id":"c370c408e71c4555a7f37ab07ec83edd","actor":{"id":"insrc:controller","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:26:37.927Z","operation":"update","revision":{"number":2,"contentHash":"553667f6febcd92bc62e2efbc85035677c07bd19b989c61d1da29a3e29208547"},"outcome":{"result":"design-review-findings-addressed","summary":"Address round1 required-neighbour loss, correction dropping, typed error bypass, provider profile preparation, raw failure logs and actual controller-state migration. Native budget preference remains open."},"addresses":"all"}}
11817	{"artifactId":"LLD-a8c4399a90185f7f-s1","entry":{"id":"review-a33bb4adde983eb3510a53631e3ec977","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:27:00.996Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed accounting, evidence preservation, generated-history filtering and telemetry address the approved issue's fix intent.","evidence":"ISSUE-ecf8440c29a6aa99 requests an inclusive budget, preserved required evidence, flat JSONL exclusion, content-free outcomes and unchanged configuration/timeouts. The LLD designs these changes and explicitly leaves the native hard-ceiling interpretation pending. [files: .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-ecf8440c29a6aa99.json]","action":"Resolve Q-native-ceiling before implementation approval; the estimated policy must not be presented as a verified native ceiling.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Current admission measures enveloped message text rather than inclusive request context.","evidence":"limit.ts defines REVIEW_CHARS_PER_TOKEN = 3 and DEFAULT_REVIEW_CHUNK_TOKENS = 128_000. job.ts compares sentChars against plan.limitChars; driver.ts supplies call.schema separately to the provider. promptChars counts text and role headings. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/limit.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/envelope.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts]","action":"Preserve promptChars as diagnostics and replace admission comparisons with the proposed shared estimator.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing planner drops required neighbours, and oversized invalid-answer corrections can be omitted on retry.","evidence":"prepare.ts repeatedly executes 'neighbours = neighbours.slice(0, -1)' when over hard. applyFailure in job.ts retains call.prompt when the corrected prompt exceeds the limit and logs 'without the correction'. Tests explicitly expect 'only the summaries that fit'. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/prepare.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/__tests__/pipeline-job.test.ts]","action":"Implement the explicit refusal paths and update all omission-expecting tests, including refusal-replanning cases.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The serial driver and managed inspection/final-answer helpers exist, while the proposed review budget contracts are new.","evidence":"runReviewJob selects calls[0] and awaits execution serially. Ollama.runReviewSession invokes runReadOnlyToolLoop followed by emitStructuredAnswer. Those helpers currently have no reviewBudget argument; searches found no ReviewBudgetPolicy, ReviewExecutionBudget or getReviewBudgetProfile implementation in the inspected application sources. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts, src/agent/providers/ollama.ts, src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts, src/shared/types.ts]","action":"Reuse these execution paths and add opt-in guards without changing non-review callers.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The change-site inventory covers controller review paths sufficiently to implement the stated all-review admission contract.","evidence":"The LLD specifies controller-reserved profiles but only concretely identifies code-review controller state. code-review-step/handler.ts builds and returns whole dimension prompts directly in emitJudgementsResult, bypassing createReviewJob. Separately, review-step/phases/start.ts returns buildTemplateReviewPrompt or buildExtractPrompt directly, and phases/claims.ts returns buildBatchedVerifyPrompt. These design-review controller emission and resume sites are absent from the inventory and have no specified budget/profile integration. [files: src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/phases/start.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/phases/claims.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/types.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/state-store.ts]","action":"Add both controller implementations to the design. Specify profile acquisition, admission before each prompt/schema emission, oversized-input handling, and budget-version validation at their actual resume boundaries. Explicitly describe the limit of host-conversation accounting.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The relationship documentation and sequence companion adequately explain the proposed internal ownership and execution boundaries.","evidence":"Section 3.3 states job-to-policy ownership, job-to-call cardinality, call-to-admission/recheck cardinality and provider copy semantics. The linked HTML contains the planner/budget/driver/provider/log sequence and descriptions. The supplied /tmp/review-budget-sequence.png visibly renders that sequence consistently with the HTML source; this verifies the supplied rendering, not a fresh browser execution. [files: docs/standalone/enforce-all-inclusive-review-budgets-exclude-E20261027a8c4399a/S001/sequence-diagram.html, /tmp/review-budget-sequence.png]","action":"Retain the ownership prose. Regenerate the companion when adding the missing controller admission boundaries; removing the generic 'recursion' note would improve clarity.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Controller tokens hold subject/grounding state rather than persisted ReviewPipelineJob objects, so no pipeline-job database migration is needed.","evidence":"CodeReviewStepStatePayload stores subject, optional grounding and run metadata. state-store.ts delegates to the shared step-state store; step-state.ts stores structured-cloned payloads in memory and documents loss on daemon restart. createReviewJob constructs an ephemeral job from a snapshot. [files: src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/types.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/state-store.ts, src/daemon/threads/step-state.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts]","action":"Version the actual controller payloads without rewriting completed artifacts. Account for both review and code-review controller states.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Flat JSONL exclusion can reuse the existing shared git filtering seam before subject construction.","evidence":"LEDGER_EXCLUDE_GLOBS currently contains '.insrc/artifacts/*.json'. changedFiles forwards excludeGlobs to staged, unstaged and range/per-unit diffs. resolveCodeReviewSubject passes this constant to changedFiles before constructing the subject. The documented git glob semantics keep '*' within one directory level. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/changed-files.ts, src/workflow/code-review/subject.ts]","action":"Add the flat JSONL glob and retain real-git tests proving nested user files remain included.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"This is a standalone dependency fix rather than an implementation of parent-HLD shared contracts.","evidence":"The approved issue metadata records 'standalone': true and 'magnitude': 'sized'. Its fixIntent explicitly excludes TU1 usage-domain changes, configuration changes and direct cloud REST. The LLD confines its proposed changes to review budgeting, filtering and diagnostics. [files: .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-ecf8440c29a6aa99.json]","action":"Keep TU1 implementation and global configuration outside this change; clarify the summary's HLD-base label to avoid implying a parent HLD.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed terminal budget-error handling addresses real generic-retry and partial-result paths.","evidence":"driver.classify treats unrecognized errors as transient. job.applyFailure retries and then applies fail-review or recording policies. structured-output.ts also catches errors other than AbortError/InputTooLargeError, logs their messages and converts them into validation failures. The LLD explicitly requires budget errors to bypass generic retries, provider retries and partial-success policies. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts, src/agent/providers/structured-output.ts]","action":"Carry the typed-error bypass through structured-output.ts as well as driver.ts, and verify identity/code preservation across provider wrappers.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing provider failure paths require sanitization beyond the newly proposed lifecycle sink.","evidence":"driver.ts logs failure.detail. CliProvider logs stall err:msg. Its runClaude/runCodex failure paths call cliExitError, which can persist complete stdout/stderr through writeCliFailureFile. structured-output.ts logs raw error messages and validation errors. These confirm the need for the LLD's downstream diagnostic audit. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts, src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts, src/agent/providers/structured-output.ts]","action":"Explicitly propagate review scope to subprocess failure-file handling and structured-output logging. Ensure review failures do not persist source-bearing stdout/stderr, and include these sinks in sentinel tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The test strategy covers the principal daemon budgeting regressions and existing lossy fallbacks.","evidence":"The acceptance mapping includes exact-cap accounting, schema normalization, inspection growth, gather/retry admission, JSONL filtering and paired telemetry. Existing pipeline-job tests exercise neighbour omission and refusal replanning; existing provider/tool-loop implementations expose the deterministic seams the proposed tests need. These are proposed tests, not evidence that the new behavior already passes. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/__tests__/pipeline-job.test.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/__tests__/code-review-source-inspection.test.ts, src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/phases/start.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/phases/claims.ts]","action":"Retain these cases and update every omission-expecting assertion. Add controller design-review start/claims/resume admission tests alongside the existing code-review controller tests to cover the missing change sites.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":0,"low":11,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T05:27:00.996Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
