10930	{"artifactId":"LLD-a8c4399a90185f7f-s1","entry":{"id":"review-7c83479ea2a94e60df613090824bed48","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:33:05.208Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers the approved issue's inclusive accounting, evidence preservation, JSONL exclusion and content-free call diagnostics without changing its stated non-goals.","evidence":"ISSUE-ecf8440c29a6aa99.fixIntent requires these changes and explicitly prohibits global configuration changes, cloud REST, prompt retention and TU1 usage-domain changes. Sections 3.1–3.12 and the migration address those requirements. The native hard-ceiling preference remains explicitly unresolved rather than represented as satisfied. [files: .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-ecf8440c29a6aa99.json]","action":"Resolve Q-native-ceiling before implementation approval, as the design already requires.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Current review admission measures enveloped message characters rather than an inclusive request budget.","evidence":"job.ts sentChars returns promptChars(envelopeMessages(...)); issue constructs the output schema separately. limit.ts multiplies review.chunkTokens by 3, defaulting to 128000. driver.ts passes messages and schema separately to the provider. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/envelope.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/limit.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts]","action":"Implement the proposed shared accounting replacement.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Required-neighbour omission, oversized-correction omission and source-bearing failure logs are existing behavior requiring correction.","evidence":"prepare.ts repeatedly executes 'neighbours = neighbours.slice(0, -1)' above the hard limit. applyFailure retains call.prompt when the corrected prompt exceeds the limit and logs reasons. driver.ts logs failure.detail derived from err.message; CliProvider.runReviewSession logs 'err: msg' on stalls. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/prepare.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts, src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts]","action":"Keep the explicit removal and sanitization requirements.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing serial driver, managed tool loop and schema normalizer provide the proposed reuse seams.","evidence":"runReviewJob dispatches calls[0] and awaits completion before continuing. runReadOnlyToolLoop accumulates assistant/tool-result blocks and calls complete each turn; emitStructuredAnswer appends its closing instruction. CliProvider.codexSchemaJson already serializes codexStrictSchema(schema). These inspected paths currently lack the proposed review budget guard. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts, src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts, src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts]","action":"Reuse these implementations while adding admission before each actual request.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The provider-owned createReviewJob production entry-point inventory is complete.","evidence":"Repository search found three production callers: runDimensionJob, grounded runReview and runTemplateReview. Reading their bodies confirms each constructs a job before runReviewJob and has the selected provider available. Section 3.6 names all three. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/code-review.ts, src/workflow/review/review.ts, src/workflow/review/template-review.ts]","action":"Resolve and freeze profiles at all three sites before planning.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The controller contract change-site inventory includes the registered input schemas and final-answer handlers that must enforce the new envelope.","evidence":"The design requires registered MCP input changes and validation before findings/verdicts completion, but its controller call-site lists omit src/mcp/server.ts and phases/findings.ts and phases/verdicts.ts. server.ts defines the actual Zod input envelopes; handleFindings currently validates input.findings and persists directly, while handleVerdicts reads input.verdicts and persists through its own path. Updating start/claims/types/stores alone does not implement these contracts. [files: src/mcp/server.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/phases/findings.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/phases/verdicts.ts]","action":"Add the registration schemas and both terminal handlers explicitly to the change inventory; specify decoding and validating callId/answer before existing validators and persistence.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Controller continuation is new state in the actual existing stores, rather than migration of persisted pipeline jobs.","evidence":"Code-review state-store saves payloads under kind 'code-review'; review state-store uses kind 'review' and updateState preserves its token. Both delegate to the shared in-memory step-state store. The inspected controller handlers retain subject/grounding or markdown/claims/evidence and do not store ReviewPipelineJob. The three daemon entry points construct fresh jobs. [files: src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/state-store.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/state-store.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/phases/start.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/phases/claims.ts, src/daemon/threads/step-state.ts]","action":"Retain explicit stale-version refusal and completed-record compatibility.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Existing state-store locking/token consumption is sufficient to reject concurrent replay of the proposed continuation.","evidence":"Section 3.12 says 'Use existing state-store locking/token-consumption behavior'. SharedStepStateStore exposes independent read/update/release operations, with no lock, claim or compare-and-swap. LocalStepStateStore.read returns the payload without consuming it. Code-review driveRunner releases the token only after awaiting runReview; design handleFindings releases only after persistReview. Two concurrent submissions can therefore read the same pending call before either advances or releases it. [files: src/daemon/threads/step-state.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/phases/findings.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/state-store.ts]","action":"Design an atomic per-token transition or handler-level serialization covering validation, call consumption and completion. Specify failure recovery that preserves state on missing declarations, and concurrent duplicate-submission tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Budget errors need an explicit terminal escape before existing retry and partial-result policies.","evidence":"driver.classify treats unrecognized errors as transient. job.applyFailure retries and then permits record-not-judged/record-observation stage policies. The proposed typed-error check before classify/applyFailure directly addresses these existing conversion paths; correction overflow is also given an explicit refusal instead of the current uncorrected retry. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts]","action":"Implement the typed escape and assert zero subsequent provider calls and zero successful partial completion.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed relationship and interaction documentation is adequate without an ERD.","evidence":"Section 3.3 specifies job/policy ownership, call/admission cardinalities, managed rechecks and event references; sections 3.10–3.12 describe controller continuation and compatibility. The linked HTML contains the planner/budget/driver/provider/event sequence. The supplied /tmp PNG renders those participants and messages consistently with that source. Its refusal path could be clearer: invocation is drawn unconditionally after 'Start or refused'. No changed product layout requires a UX mock. [files: docs/standalone/enforce-all-inclusive-review-budgets-exclude-E20261027a8c4399a/S001/sequence-diagram.html, /tmp/review-budget-sequence.png]","action":"Optionally add an admitted/refused branch and a controller continuation sequence. I inspected the existing PNG and HTML source; I did not freshly render the current HTML.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The test strategy maps the stated acceptance areas to meaningful regression cases using existing test seams.","evidence":"The design maps ac1–ac6 to accounting, evidence preservation, provider qualification, filtering, telemetry and compatibility tests. pipeline-job.test.ts already exercises all three failure policies, correction retries, neighbour omission and deadlines; controller handlers expose deterministic state and injected runner seams. The proposed boundary and sentinel tests would detect behavior absent from current code. This checks test design, not execution of unimplemented tests. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/__tests__/pipeline-job.test.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/phases/findings.ts]","action":"Add concurrent same-token/same-call submissions to the controller test matrix when correcting the state-transition design.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":1,"low":9,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T05:33:05.208Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
