12057	{"artifactId":"LLD-a8c4399a90185f7f-s1","entry":{"id":"review-7be85f6dc2f6adf8a379ae76336d8acc","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:49:11.260Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers the approved dependency fix and the subsequent chunk-scaled timing instruction.","evidence":"ISSUE-ecf8440c29a6aa99 requests inclusive accounting, evidence preservation, flat JSONL exclusion and content-free call outcomes. Sections 3.1–3.17 address these and explicitly incorporate the supplied 10×chunk timing instruction. The native hard-ceiling interpretation remains explicitly unresolved rather than falsely guaranteed. [files: .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-ecf8440c29a6aa99.json]","action":"Resolve Q-native-ceiling before implementation approval, as the design requires.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Current planning omits separate schema costs and can drop required neighbours and oversized corrections.","evidence":"job.ts measures promptChars(envelopeMessages(...)) while storing the schema separately. prepare.ts removes neighbours using 'neighbours = neighbours.slice(0, -1)'. applyFailure retains the original prompt when the correction exceeds the limit and logs 'without the correction'. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/prepare.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/envelope.ts]","action":"Implement the explicit fail-closed replacements specified in sections 3.7–3.8.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Ten-minute per-attempt limits are unchanged across the covered review paths.","evidence":"template.ts defines 'HARD_REVIEW_DEADLINE_MS = 30 * 60_000' and design-review defaults of 12, 18 and 24 minutes. job.ts caps reviewer-session limits against that 30-minute constant. pipeline-job.test.ts explicitly expects 'no session runs longer than 30 minutes'. A universal ten-minute attempt cap is therefore a behavior change, not preservation of the existing contract. [files: src/workflow/review/template.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/__tests__/pipeline-job.test.ts]","action":"Describe the ten-minute cap as an explicit change for design review, distinguish it from existing code-review defaults, and identify the affected settings/helper semantics and regression updates.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The serial planner/driver and provider schema normalizer are valid reuse targets; managed inspection requires a new budget guard.","evidence":"runReviewJob dispatches only calls[0] in its loop. codexStrictSchema produces a normalized copy and rejects unsupported formats/dangling references. runReadOnlyToolLoop accumulates assistant/tool-result messages and emitStructuredAnswer appends the closing instruction, with no existing inclusive admission guard. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts, src/agent/providers/structured-output.ts, src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts]","action":"Reuse these paths and ensure the guard measures their actual final serialization.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The atomic ownership proposal identifies complete integration sites for trusted worker/request ownership and owner-loss invalidation.","evidence":"channel.ts defines 'HubHandler = (args: unknown) => unknown'; serveHub invokes handler(msg.args), without authenticated channel/request ownership. main-services.ts installs one shared handler set and connectWorker.disconnect only stops/closes the port. supervisor.ts handles worker exit through router.detach and worker.disconnect; router.ts owns request cancellation. These lifecycle integration files are absent from sections 3.13–3.15's change inventory, and no concrete trusted owner binding or invalidation hook is specified. Adding store operations alone cannot deliver the promised owner-loss behavior; pinned abandoned claims can remain busy indefinitely. [files: src/daemon/threads/channel.ts, src/daemon/threads/main-services.ts, src/daemon/threads/supervisor.ts, src/daemon/threads/router.ts, src/daemon/threads/step-state.ts]","action":"Specify trusted channel plus request ownership propagation and explicit invalidation hooks in main-services.ts, supervisor.ts and router/request lifecycle handling, including the single-thread path. Add these change sites and tests that exercise real worker exit/cancellation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing production createReviewJob callers are identified.","evidence":"Repository-wide caller search finds the three production entries named by section 3.6: runDimensionJob, grounded review and template review. Other direct callers are tests. The current controller code independently emits prompts, confirming that its separately listed integration is necessary. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/code-review.ts, src/workflow/review/review.ts, src/workflow/review/template-review.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts]","action":"Update all three entries and the controller emissions together.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Controller continuation is new ephemeral state requiring explicit version rejection, rather than migration of persisted pipeline jobs.","evidence":"ReviewStepStatePayload stores markdown, intent, claims and evidence, not ReviewPipelineJob. Its state-store delegates to the shared in-memory store. The shared store documents restart loss and distinct stable-token/consume-per-stage lifecycles. The design explicitly rejects old tokens and legacy reply envelopes while preserving completed artifacts. [files: src/daemon/steps/review-step/types.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/state-store.ts, src/daemon/threads/step-state.ts]","action":"Implement the declared stale-token refusal and keep missing-declaration validation non-consuming.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Flat JSONL exclusion can reuse the existing shared changed-file seam before subject/freshness selection.","evidence":"LEDGER_EXCLUDE_GLOBS currently includes '.insrc/artifacts/*.json'. changedFiles forwards excludeGlobs to its diff derivations. subject.ts passes LEDGER_EXCLUDE_GLOBS when deriving changedFiles before constructing the review subject. Adding the flat JSONL glob preserves the existing deliberate nested-file distinction. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/changed-files.ts, src/workflow/code-review/subject.ts]","action":"Retain the proposed real-git staged, unstaged, attributed-range and nested-user-file regressions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Relationship documentation adequately describes the new budget ownership without requiring an ERD.","evidence":"Section 3.3 specifies one job owning one policy, 0..N calls, one admission per call, managed-turn rechecks and immutable provider copies. Sections 3.13–3.14 describe claim ownership and generations. The linked HTML source and supplied PNG show the planner→budget→driver→provider interaction. The rendered PNG displays the sequence, although current HTML was not freshly rendered. The source contains an unexplained 'Note over budget: recursion' corresponding to a recurse label in its description. [files: docs/standalone/enforce-all-inclusive-review-budgets-exclude-E20261027a8c4399a/S001/sequence-diagram.html, /tmp/review-budget-sequence.png]","action":"Optionally remove the irrelevant recursion note and regenerate the companion. A controller claim/commit sequence would improve readability, but the prose supplies the necessary relationships.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Typed budget refusals must bypass the current generic retry and partial-result policies.","evidence":"driver.ts classifies unrecognized exceptions as transient and forwards them to applyFailure. job.ts retries and can record notJudged instead of throwing. driver.ts also logs failure.detail derived from err.message, while job.ts logs raw correction reasons. The proposed early typed-error propagation and sanitization address concrete failure paths. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts, src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts]","action":"Retain explicit tests for every stage failure policy and capture existing provider/driver/job loggers, not only the new event callback.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Existing verdict handlers already enforce claim-ID completeness, as section 3.15 implies.","evidence":"handleVerdicts reads 'input.verdicts?.verdicts ?? []', loops only over supplied entries, drops unknown claim IDs and persists the resulting findings. It never requires every state claim exactly once or rejects duplicate verdict IDs. An empty response can therefore reach report construction and persistence. Merely preserving 'existing claim-ID completeness' does not provide the promised complete review. [files: src/daemon/steps/review-step/phases/verdicts.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/types.ts]","action":"Explicitly add exact expected-claim-set validation to the terminal handler and continuation aggregation: reject missing, duplicate and unknown claim IDs before persistence. Test empty and partial verdict arrays as well as mismatched call IDs.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed test plan maps the acceptance criteria to relevant existing regression seams.","evidence":"The acceptance table maps ac1–ac7 to accounting, evidence-preserving subdivision, provider qualification/history growth, real-git exclusion, paired sanitized outcomes, compatibility and fake-clock timing. Existing pipeline-job tests explicitly cover neighbour omission and frozen subdivision deadlines, matching the tests the design proposes to change. Existing state tests and hub helpers are appropriate foundations for the new concurrency cases. This verifies test-plan coverage, not execution of unimplemented tests. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/__tests__/pipeline-job.test.ts, src/daemon/threads/__tests__/step-state.test.ts, src/daemon/threads/__tests__/helpers/step-state-worker.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/phases/verdicts.ts]","action":"Add the concrete owner-loss integration and exact verdict claim-set cases identified above to the acceptance mapping.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":2,"med":1,"low":9,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T05:49:11.260Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
