13108	{"artifactId":"LLD-a8c4399a90185f7f-s1","entry":{"id":"review-98a92f8aba75bb331311f86175a367d1","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:58:42.329Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers the approved issue's inclusive accounting, evidence preservation, JSONL exclusion and diagnostic requirements, plus the explicitly supplied chunk-scaled timing instruction.","evidence":"ISSUE-ecf8440c29a6aa99 requests one inclusive policy across initial/retry/gather/comparison calls, preservation of required evidence, flat JSONL exclusion and content-free call outcomes. Sections 3.1–3.21 address those requirements. The supplied stakeholder instruction explicitly authorizes replacing the issue's original unchanged-total-time requirement with 10 minutes per chunk. [files: .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-ecf8440c29a6aa99.json]","action":"Resolve Q-native-ceiling before implementation approval, as the design requires.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing planning measures serialized prompt text rather than an inclusive context allowance, and contains the two described evidence/correction omission fallbacks.","evidence":"limit.ts defines REVIEW_CHARS_PER_TOKEN=3 and DEFAULT_REVIEW_CHUNK_TOKENS=128_000. job.ts measures promptChars(envelopeMessages(...)) while issuing the schema separately. prepare.ts repeatedly executes 'neighbours = neighbours.slice(0, -1)' on overflow. applyFailure keeps call.prompt when its corrected replacement exceeds limitChars and logs that it is reissuing without the correction. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/limit.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/envelope.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/prepare.ts]","action":"Implement the explicitly designed replacements; do not characterize existing packing as wholly evidence-preserving.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Current reviewer-session total deadlines are frozen from the initial session count, and design-review limits differ from code-review defaults.","evidence":"job.ts returns immediately when deadlineAt already exists and initially calculates sessionLimitMs*sessions.length. template.ts defines 12/18/24-minute defaults and a 30-minute hard maximum; template-review.ts closes its timeout message over limitMs. The existing pipeline-job test explicitly asserts that subdivision does not extend the deadline. Section 3.21 accurately identifies these as contracts requiring deliberate change. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts, src/workflow/review/template.ts, src/workflow/review/template-review.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/__tests__/pipeline-job.test.ts]","action":"Update both behavior and the existing deadline assertions as specified.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing serial job engine, envelope validation, schema normalization and managed tool loop are suitable reuse points; inclusive admission and atomic review claims are additions.","evidence":"runReviewJob dispatches calls serially with internalRetry:false. openEnvelope requires the expected callId. CliProvider serializes codexStrictSchema(schema). runReadOnlyToolLoop retains conversation/tool results and emitStructuredAnswer appends a closing instruction. SharedStepStateStore currently exposes independent mint/read/update/release operations rather than claim/commit. The analyzer returned an explicitly incomplete graph bundle; these conclusions rely on the inspected implementations rather than graph completeness. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/envelope.ts, src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts, src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts, src/daemon/threads/step-state.ts]","action":"Keep normalization shared with actual serialization and preserve existing non-review loop behavior.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design identifies the production job constructors and actual controller/schema boundaries that must participate in admission.","evidence":"Production createReviewJob calls occur in review-pipeline/code-review.ts, review/review.ts and review/template-review.ts, all named in section 3.6. emitJudgementsResult returns the computed dimension prompts, schema, grounding and token together. server.ts registers the actual claims/verdicts/findings/judgements envelopes, and handleFindings/handleVerdicts consume their raw answer fields today. Sections 3.10–3.15 explicitly include these boundaries and their bypass prevention. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/code-review.ts, src/workflow/review/review.ts, src/workflow/review/template-review.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/phases/findings.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/phases/verdicts.ts, src/mcp/server.ts]","action":"Apply combined-frame admission to every computed dimension, including optional functional-coverage, diagram and UX dimensions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed relationships have sufficient ownership and compatibility documentation without requiring an ERD.","evidence":"Section 3.3 specifies one job owning one policy, 0..N calls, one admission per call, managed rechecks and provider copy ownership. Sections 3.13–3.19 specify main-thread ownership, connection/request binding, claim generations, completion receipts and owner-loss transitions. The linked sequence source describes planner-to-policy-to-driver-to-provider accounting. The saved PNG visibly renders that basic sequence. [files: docs/standalone/enforce-all-inclusive-review-budgets-exclude-E20261027a8c4399a/S001/sequence-diagram.html, /tmp/review-budget-sequence.png]","action":"Optionally extend the sequence companion to illustrate controller claim/commit and owner loss; the detailed prose already defines those relationships.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The current linked HTML's rendering has been independently verified for this revision.","evidence":"Inspected the HTML's embedded Mermaid source and the existing /tmp/review-budget-sequence.png. The saved capture demonstrates a rendered version of the basic sequence, but no fresh browser render was performed to establish the current HTML's visual output or revision correspondence. [files: docs/standalone/enforce-all-inclusive-review-budgets-exclude-E20261027a8c4399a/S001/sequence-diagram.html, /tmp/review-budget-sequence.png]","action":"Render the current companion and inspect it before claiming current-revision visual verification.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Controller continuation migration belongs in the existing ephemeral step stores, with explicit protocol rejection rather than rewriting completed artifacts or migrating stored pipeline jobs.","evidence":"Both controller state-store modules use getStepStateStore with review/code-review kinds. step-state.ts keeps payloads in in-memory maps; review tokens are stable and code-review tokens consume per stage. Existing wrappers describe subject/grounding or review run state, not persisted pipeline jobs. The proposed version/profile fields, stale-token refusal and bounded receipts directly address these actual storage semantics and disclose client incompatibility. [files: src/daemon/threads/step-state.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/state-store.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/state-store.ts]","action":"Preserve the distinct per-kind token rules when adding atomic transitions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The shared-store and channel additions are explicitly scoped to review ownership rather than replacing unrelated token or connection execution contracts.","evidence":"SharedStepStateStore serves analyze, workflow, review and code-review with different lifecycle rules. channel.ts currently invokes HubHandler with args alone, while wireRequest explicitly rejects connectionSession/connectionExecution capabilities crossing workers. Sections 3.13 and 3.18 preserve unrelated lifecycle behavior and that refusal, introducing only opaque review owner metadata through trusted internal carriers. ThreadServices.connectWorker is correctly identified as the connection-binding seam. [files: src/daemon/threads/step-state.ts, src/daemon/threads/channel.ts, src/daemon/threads/main-services.ts, src/shared/step-context.ts]","action":"Retain regression tests for analyze/workflow tokens and the existing capability serialization refusal.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design explicitly replaces generic retry/partial-result conversion and source-bearing logging for budget failures.","evidence":"driver.ts currently classifies unrecognized errors as transient and logs failure.detail derived from err.message. job.ts can turn exhausted calls into notJudged according to stage policy and logs raw correction reasons. CliProvider.runReviewSession logs raw stall messages before rethrow. Sections 3.8–3.9 require typed budget errors to bypass these branches and sanitize existing provider/driver logs, not merely new events. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts, src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts]","action":"Keep the sentinel tests spanning existing downstream diagnostics and every failure policy, as specified.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design correctly treats exact verdict coverage and atomic finalization as new safeguards, with explicit failure and recovery behavior.","evidence":"handleVerdicts uses 'input.verdicts?.verdicts ?? []', iterates only submitted entries, drops unknown IDs and then persists; it does not reject missing or duplicate claims. Both terminal design handlers load state before awaited persistence and release afterward. The store supplies no exclusive claim. Sections 3.13–3.20 explicitly add exact assigned/global coverage, exclusive claims, uncertain-state invalidation, completion receipts and zero-write rejection paths. [files: src/daemon/steps/review-step/phases/verdicts.ts, src/daemon/steps/review-step/phases/findings.ts, src/daemon/threads/step-state.ts]","action":"Implement the real handler/worker lifecycle tests, including concurrent final submissions and ambiguous persistence.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed test strategy maps the intended acceptance behaviors to appropriate existing seams and explicitly revises conflicting historical assertions.","evidence":"Existing pipeline-job tests already use injected clocks and scripted providers and assert frozen subdivision deadlines, retry remaining-time clamps and cancellation. step-state.test.ts already exercises real MessageChannel/Worker transport and per-kind TTL/capacity behavior. Section 6 adds inclusive boundaries, schema normalization, managed-history growth, real-git filtering, terminal telemetry, exact coverage, concurrent persistence and real owner-loss hooks; its acceptance mapping covers ac1–ac7. These are design-level test commitments, not claims that new tests already pass. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/__tests__/pipeline-job.test.ts, src/daemon/threads/__tests__/step-state.test.ts, package.json]","action":"Implement the listed regressions and run focused suites plus the production build; no implementation tests were run during this document review.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":12,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T05:58:42.329Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
